decision=observed
identity=prozess-reflexion-04
intent=Das Vorhaben aus prozess-reflexion-03 aufgreifen: denselben Wunsch einmal mit blind und einmal mit lesend geschriebenem Gate messen, und den Stand nach der Nacht festhalten.
scope=2026-11-26, 03:35 to 03:50. One request (auftragsbericht: option --json) was sent twice to the orchestrator for the repository auftragsbericht. For the first the reading gate author was marked as failed by hand, so that an agent without access to the repository wrote the gate (pi-grok). For the second the reading author wrote it (pruefer, Sonnet 5.5). Both sessions started from the same commit of the repository and ran side by side with the same worker (Opus 5.5). Costs are list prices.
measured_pair_2=Blind gate, job-ticket-034: 2 rounds, 1 rejected, 0.85 USD, 94 s of worker time. Reading gate, job-ticket-035: 1 round, 0 rejected, 0.46 USD, 98 s.
measured_pair_1=From prozess-reflexion-03: blind gate, job-ticket-008: 5 rounds rejected, 9.24 USD, closed. Reading gate, job-ticket-009: 1 round, 1.14 USD.
finding=In both pairs the job with the reading gate author was accepted in round 1 and the job with the blind gate author was not. The cost of the blind job was 1.8 and 8.1 times that of the reading one. Two pairs with one worker model on two repositories; no statistical claim.
cause_in_pair_2=The rejected round of job-ticket-034 failed on the last line of the gate's own fixture run, which printed the unchanged text output. The agent changed its work in round 2 and passed. Whether the first candidate was wrong or the gate's expectation was, the record does not show; the gate printed no reason.
not_measured=The time and cost of writing the gates themselves. The reading author runs a session with file tools and is more expensive per gate than a call without tools; its ledger lies in STATE/requests and is not part of these numbers.
state_after_the_night=35 requests went through the orchestrator. Of the jobs that started from them, 28 ended accepted and 1 was closed. 9 changes of the core were landed from session jobs, the last two by the repository's own procedure .taik/land.sh. 12 changes of the viewer were released by the service. The gate of the product ansicht holds 9 checks that jobs added; each failed on the viewer before its job. Every button of the viewer is pressed by the WebKit check and every message is handled by the freshly built app in its gate. No person has used the app yet.
not_shown=Work the Factory proposed by itself. Its reflection now goes through the orchestrator, but the daily limit of three was used up by test reflections of the day before. G-03, I-01 and I-03 of the specification stay not established.
continuation=When the daily limit is free again, let one job finish and read what the Factory proposes from its own open intents. Have the gate of a session print the reason of a failure, as the contract for its author already demands.
end
